{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan","id":949130,"title":"What's up with the Ulgan?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-11T22:33:50-07:00","id":949130,"title":"What's up with the Ulgan?","content":"Maybe this is coming from the fact that I didn't read Promethean 1e, but I am very confused about the Ulgans' relationship with ephemeral entities. It's clear that they are deeply connected to Twilight, but it seems extremely inconsistent whether this connection is meant to be with ephemeral entities in general, or spirits specifically, or spirits and ghosts but not other EEs, or what.<br /> <br /> A great deal of the text concerning Ulgan incorrectly treats Twilight like a place, which I've made note of in the errata thread, but moreover, it seems like in some places they're specifically connected with spirits, as in the animistic entities native to the shadow, while other times it seems more like it's using &quot;spirit&quot; as a catch-all term for any sort of EE. To confuse matters further, their humour is called ectoplasm, which in Mage and Geist is something specifically connected to ghosts, but the Ulgan generally seem to be more associated with spirits than with ghosts. For example, the Extempore writeup recommends a focus on ghosts over spirits as a way to differentiate Extempore with an excess of ectoplasmic humor from Ulgan, saying; &quot;Extempore tied to ectoplasm might be more closely died to the ghosts of the dead than the spirits of the natural world, with an accompanying difference in character.&quot; But then the section on Ulgan Bestowments is completely focused on ghosts with no mention of spirits, saying, &quot;Whereas Osirans tease at the line between the living and the dead, Ulgan revel in the macabre. They\u2019re death warmed over and maintain strong ties to the Underworld. Ghosts, the hungry dead, shades: these are all kin to the Ulgan.&quot;<br /> <br /> Can anyone help shed some light on this for me? What exactly is the Ulgans' relationship with the ephemeral supposed to be? Are they Spirit Masters? Ghost Whisperers? Ephemeral Entity Generalists? Does their affinity for Twilight entities extend to Angels, or Goetia? What the heck is their deal and why do they seem so inconsistent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-12-2016, 02:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T22:50:59-07:00","id":949140,"title":"","content":"The Ulgan in 1e were specifically aimed at dealing with spirits, and were generally treated as sacrifices-turned-shamans who found themselves harried by spirits at every turn. I didn't really care for them because using spirits to learn about humanity seemed a little bit silly, and also because I was bitter that they broke from the four traditional humours. One of the later books suggested the idea of 'Orphean' variant Ulgan who deal with ghosts rather than spirits, That still didn't really scratch the itch for me because the Osirans were already our 'deal with the dead' Lineage.<br /> <br /> So the Ulgan are a little weird for me, and it seems like 2e has only muddled things a little more. I don't really have a good answer for you, other than that I might love to see a constellation of ephemeral-focused Lineages; one each for spirits, ghosts, and anything else out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-12-2016, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T23:21:04-07:00","id":949155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan#post949130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone help shed some light on this for me? What exactly is the Ulgans' relationship with the ephemeral supposed to be? Are they Spirit Nasters? Ghost Whisperers? Ephemeral Entity Generalists? Does their affinity for Twilight entities extend to Angels, or Goetia? What the heck is their deal and why do they seem so inconsistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghosts, Spirits, and G-M Angels are all &quot;ephemeral entities&quot; of the same immaterial substance (hence the shared use of Essence) that the Ulgans pump through themselves as their dominant humour. The Riven do not resonate with the different origins of these entities, they resonate with their common substance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T23:23:37-07:00","id":949156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949140#post949140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and also because I was bitter that they broke from the four traditional humours.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying them to the fifth element of the same Greek philosophy that ties the four humours to the other four, and Descartean &quot;pineal gland&quot; pseudo-biology, made them fit pretty well IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T04:12:07-07:00","id":949228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan#post949130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this is coming from the fact that I didn't read Promethean 1e, but I am very confused about the Ulgans' relationship with ephemeral entities. It's clear that they are deeply connected to Twilight, but it seems extremely inconsistent whether this connection is meant to be with ephemeral entities in general, or spirits specifically, or spirits and ghosts but not other EEs, or what.</div> </div> </div> </div> Something to keep in mind. Remember, this game came out when the only ephemeral entities were ghosts and spirits, plus the brand new qashmal. Nothing like the strix, no angels, and while goetic demons existed, they were considered to be a form of spirit. There were astral projections, but that's rare enough to be negligable. And the qashmal, well, they're pretty rare and show up and leave as plot points, not really long term NPCs. So, 1e formed around using the only two entites that were available at the time, and that carried forwards.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to point out that, at the time of Promethean, there was kind of a trend from White Wolf books to use the <i>Hisil </i> for anything related to spirits in general, not just animistic spirits. Vampire summoners? <i>Hisil</i>, go! Ephemeral Prometheans? Use the Shadow! Mage summoners all used the Shadow, even when they wanted an abrahamic themed angel as well! A lot of books at this time had that kind of feeling to them. The nWoD was still heavily tied to the cWoD cosmological mindset and hadn't quite broken away yet to make its own thing. In fact, Promethean was probably the very first step, and continued with Changeling, which moved towards the &quot;everyone with their own playground&quot; model instead.<br /> <br /> So, a good chunk of the Ulgan are based around the trend of fifth element = spirit = <i>Hisil </i>that was coming off the current mindset of the game. And it kind of just got ingrained. And the focus on spirits over ghosts was naturally the result of the <i>Hisil</i> being far more developed than anything related to ghosts. Despite being in the WoD core, ghosts were kind of ignored for a long time in 1e and had little material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A great deal of the text concerning Ulgan incorrectly treats Twilight like a place, which I've made note of in the errata thread, but moreover, it seems like in some places they're specifically connected with spirits, as in the animistic entities native to the shadow, while other times it seems more like it's using &quot;spirit&quot; as a catch-all term for any sort of EE. </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Mage does the same thing. Especially when you create portals into it. Treating Twilight as a pseudo-realm is actually pretty common.<br /> <br /> And, yeah, using &quot;spirit&quot; as a general term for ephemeral entities is kind of common too. Its hard sometimes, because the overwhelming majority of writers we have for the game aren't technical writers, and to be frank, the CofD games deliberately don't nail down definitions and key words in a lot of cases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To confuse matters further, their humour is called ectoplasm, which in Mage and Geist is something specifically connected to ghosts, but the Ulgan generally seem to be more associated with spirits than with ghosts. </div> </div> </div> Geist wasn't even a proposal yet, and Mage 1e's use of ectoplasm actually supports calling the Ulgan element ectoplasm. At this point, ectoplasm was treated as &quot;unliving&quot; ephemera. You used it to shape ephemeral tools and houses and the like. Literally the building blocks of spiritual objects. The Elemental Tamer of the Cave Legacy also used ectoplasm as their element.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Extempore writeup </div> </div> </div> Extempore are basically just a universal variation of the core five Lineages under the umbrella of being the &quot;super customizable Lineage.&quot; I wouldn't put too much faith in this as something to compare against.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can anyone help shed some light on this for me? What exactly is the Ulgans' relationship with the ephemeral supposed to be? Are they Spirit Masters? Ghost Whisperers? Ephemeral Entity Generalists? Does their affinity for Twilight entities extend to Angels, or Goetia? What the heck is their deal and why do they seem so inconsistent? </div> </div> </div> They're meant to be &quot;constructs made of Spirit matter.&quot; They're not spirit masters or mediums, they're machines made from ephemera and shoved into flesh. Each 1e Lineage is powered by an element - fire (electricity, but hey), wind, water, earth and hea... spirit. Ulgan are just constructs powered by spirits. They learn about humanity from watching and observing how the spirits and ghosts form around humans.<br /> <br /> There's no spirit master, no ghost whispering. In fact, there's no real drive to deal with these entities other than a source of answers and companionship - ghosts and spirits aren't affected by Disquiet, and the former still remembers what its like to be human while the latter often are the products of human life. This makes them a good source of information about any questions about humanity you might have almost right from the source.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> That said, for many players the Ulgan remained very strange and an odd fit. They felt forced in to fit the 5x5 model, especially when the game didn't even provide any spirit-related or ghost-related abilities until after the core (I forget when Silver came out). Ulgans who followed a Refinement other than Copper or Silver really didn't have any drive or desire to deal with spirits in a lot of cases - spirits generally don't help out with the study of pyros or body building. In a very real way, Ulgans feel inconsistant because they're pseudo-shaman outcasts that don't quite fit into a game that doesn't deal with other supernaturals well. They don't quite match up because spirit specialists don't quite fit into a game that focuses primarily on human nature. Its hard to include the Hisil in a game that overwhelmingly doesn't care about the Shadow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-12-2016, 07:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:44:18-07:00","id":949282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949228#post949228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Something to keep in mind. Remember, this game came out when the only ephemeral entities were ghosts and spirits, plus the brand new qashmal. Nothing like the strix, no angels, and while goetic demons existed, they were considered to be a form of spirit. There were astral projections, but that's rare enough to be negligable. And the qashmal, well, they're pretty rare and show up and leave as plot points, not really long term NPCs. So, 1e formed around using the only two entites that were available at the time, and that carried forwards.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd like to point out that, at the time of Promethean, there was kind of a trend from White Wolf books to use the <i>Hisil </i> for anything related to spirits in general, not just animistic spirits. Vampire summoners? <i>Hisil</i>, go! Ephemeral Prometheans? Use the Shadow! Mage summoners all used the Shadow, even when they wanted an abrahamic themed angel as well! A lot of books at this time had that kind of feeling to them. The nWoD was still heavily tied to the cWoD cosmological mindset and hadn't quite broken away yet to make its own thing. In fact, Promethean was probably the very first step, and continued with Changeling, which moved towards the &quot;everyone with their own playground&quot; model instead.<br /> <br /> So, a good chunk of the Ulgan are based around the trend of fifth element = spirit = <i>Hisil </i>that was coming off the current mindset of the game. And it kind of just got ingrained. And the focus on spirits over ghosts was naturally the result of the <i>Hisil</i> being far more developed than anything related to ghosts. Despite being in the WoD core, ghosts were kind of ignored for a long time in 1e and had little material.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explains why the 1e version was highly spirit focused, but not why 2e hasn't fixed the issue. Ephemeral Entities are far better defined now, I would expect the new edition of Promethean to be written with the 2e ephemeral entities model in mind, not to regress to the more inconsistent style of early 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949228#post949228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Mage does the same thing. Especially when you create portals into it. Treating Twilight as a pseudo-realm is actually pretty common.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the advance PDF, yeah, but according to the errata document they'll be fixing that in the final release.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949228#post949228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, yeah, using &quot;spirit&quot; as a general term for ephemeral entities is kind of common too. Its hard sometimes, because the overwhelming majority of writers we have for the game aren't technical writers, and to be frank, the CofD games deliberately don't nail down definitions and key words in a lot of cases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but isn't that something the developers should address and ask them to change in second drafts?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949228#post949228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist wasn't even a proposal yet, and Mage 1e's use of ectoplasm actually supports calling the Ulgan element ectoplasm. At this point, ectoplasm was treated as &quot;unliving&quot; ephemera. You used it to shape ephemeral tools and houses and the like. Literally the building blocks of spiritual objects. The Elemental Tamer of the Cave Legacy also used ectoplasm as their element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but Geist exists <i>now</i>, and Mage 2e's use of ectoplasm has it specifically tied to the Death Arcanum and the Twilight frequency of ghosts. &quot;1e took a while to figure out its own metaphysics&quot; is not a good excuse for a 2e game to not be consistent with 2e metaphysics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949228#post949228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Extempore are basically just a universal variation of the core five Lineages under the umbrella of being the &quot;super customizable Lineage.&quot; I wouldn't put too much faith in this as something to compare against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah, wait a second here, let's not just brush over this. Customizable lineage or not, the fact is, &quot;more associated with ghosts than spirits&quot; is a listed example of how to make a variation on the ectoplasm Humour that differs from the default for Ulgan. Which is fine, but then another passage later in the book talks about Ulgan as though they're specifically associated with ghosts. Any way you slice it, that's inconsistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949228#post949228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're meant to be &quot;constructs made of Spirit matter.&quot; They're not spirit masters or mediums, they're machines made from ephemera and shoved into flesh. Each 1e Lineage is powered by an element - fire (electricity, but hey), wind, water, earth and hea... spirit. Ulgan are just constructs powered by spirits. They learn about humanity from watching and observing how the spirits and ghosts form around humans.<br /> <br /> There's no spirit master, no ghost whispering. In fact, there's no real drive to deal with these entities other than a source of answers and companionship - ghosts and spirits aren't affected by Disquiet, and the former still remembers what its like to be human while the latter often are the products of human life. This makes them a good source of information about any questions about humanity you might have almost right from the source.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I see. So they're supposed to be associated with <i>ephemera</i> as a substance or &quot;element&quot;, not with ephemeral <i>entities</i>. That makes a lot more sense to me, thank you for clarifying. I don't think this comes through very well in the writing, and since ephemera comes in a wide variety of frequencies, I think the book would do well to be more clear on if they are supposed to all be associated with a single Twilight frequency, or they can be associated with any. I also think if they're not specifically supposed to be associated with the ghostly frequency of Twilight, then ephemera would be a better name for their Humour than ectoplasm. But that last bit is a nitpick I'd be more willing to overlook. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949228#post949228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> That said, for many players the Ulgan remained very strange and an odd fit. They felt forced in to fit the 5x5 model, especially when the game didn't even provide any spirit-related or ghost-related abilities until after the core (I forget when Silver came out). Ulgans who followed a Refinement other than Copper or Silver really didn't have any drive or desire to deal with spirits in a lot of cases - spirits generally don't help out with the study of pyros or body building. In a very real way, Ulgans feel inconsistant because they're pseudo-shaman outcasts that don't quite fit into a game that doesn't deal with other supernaturals well. They don't quite match up because spirit specialists don't quite fit into a game that focuses primarily on human nature. Its hard to include the Hisil in a game that overwhelmingly doesn't care about the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I definitely got the impression that they were just tossed in to fit the 5x5 model. The thing is, I would have expected 2e to nail their role down more, not keep them just as wishy-washy as they were in 1e. 2e has very clearly defined and consistent ephemeral entity metaphysics, and isn't a slave to the 5x5 model. The 5x5 model doesn't fly as a justification for the Ulgan's existence any more, especially because Promethean 2e isn't even 5x5, so they should be working harder to justify themselves as an X-splat. But they don't seem to be doing that, their presentation is still inconsistent and forced, and so far the only explanation I've seen is, &quot;well, they were awkward in 1e too.&quot; Isn't part of the point of a second edition to fix the places where the first edition was awkward?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-12-2016, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T07:22:42-07:00","id":949295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949282#post949282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That explains why the 1e version was highly spirit focused, but not why 2e hasn't fixed the issue. Ephemeral Entities are far better defined now, I would expect the new edition of Promethean to be written with the 2e ephemeral entities model in mind, not to regress to the more inconsistent style of early 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, you have to understand that because of the 1e version's focus on spirits, the Ulgan was given a pseudo-shaman vibe over time. A revisal of the Ulgan will reise a huge chunk of the Lineage. So, the question becomes - how much of a change do you have before it becomes something completely different? And how desirable is it to make those changes and remove a character splat as opposed to keeping it as is? The writers decided to keep the shaman part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the advance PDF, yeah, but according to the errata document they'll be fixing that in the final release. </div> </div> </div> Well, I don't know about that. If its something that's firmly being changed, then its something that should be errata'd here as well. We're probably dealing with writer confusion, due to 1) constant confusion throughout multiple books, and 2) crossover from cWoD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, but isn't that something the developers should address and ask them to change in second drafts? </div> </div> </div> Maybe? The CofD isn't a highly technical game in the first place - it has a high focus on natural language.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but Geist exists <i>now</i>, and Mage 2e's use of ectoplasm has it specifically tied to the Death Arcanum and the Twilight frequency of ghosts. &quot;1e took a while to figure out its own metaphysics&quot; is not a good excuse for a 2e game to not be consistent with 2e metaphysics. </div> </div> </div> I said the same thing about Mage 2e being stuck in 1e's metaphysics, and the answer back to me was &quot;that's just crossover stuff, and doesn't matter.&quot; I think the same kind of thought process is applying here.<br /> <br /> As near as I can tell, 2e is updating individual game lines to be internally consistant with the new rules and changes via game line supplements, and the rest of the so-called metaphysics (remember that each game line is technically stand alone) don't really apply. They're updating the game as it was writen before all those earlier changes.<br /> <br /> Now, I do agree with you that there should be greater changes made. I think that some of the game lines coming out are doubling down on mistakes and oWoD carryovers instead of updating everything to the new, general CofD design. But I get the feeling that's not the design goal here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Woah, wait a second here, let's not just brush over this. Customizable lineage or not, the fact that &quot;more associated with ghosts than spirits&quot; is a listed example of how to make a variation that differs from the default for Ulgan. Which is fine, but then another passage later in the book talks about Ulgan as though they're specifically associated with ghosts. Any way you slice it, that's inconsistent. </div> </div> </div> From what I can tell, it was an attempt to make a more sin-eater-necromancer-esk type as opposed to the werewolf-esk-shaman style that the Ulgan currently has. Mind you, shamans deal heavily with ghosts too, so its kind of a moot point. In theory, it is absolutely possible to have a more Underworld focused prommie, but that doesn't change that the Ulgan deals with ghosts as well. Not exclusively (I didn't get that impression from the Bestowments), but ghosts are there.<br /> <br /> And honestly, I think that's just a question of writer style and impression. I assume we're talking about two different writers. So, yes, I do think it should be brushed over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, I see. So they're supposed to be associated with <i>ephemera</i> as a substance or &quot;element&quot;, not with ephemeral <i>entities</i>. That makes a lot more sense to me, thank you for clarifying. I don't think this comes through very well in the writing, and since ephemera comes in a wide variety of frequencies, I think the book would do well to be more clear on if they are supposed to all be associated with a single Twilight frequency, or they can be associated with any. I also think if they're not specifically supposed to be associated with the ghostly frequency of Twilight, then ephemera would be a better name for their Humour than ectoplasm. But that last bit is a nitpick I'd be more willing to overlook. </div> </div> </div> Well, the whole &quot;Lineage elements&quot; has really been downplayed a lot in 2e to the point that it only comes up when talking about regaining pyros. So, without 1e's understanding of the matter, I can see where it would feel off. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, I definitely got the impression that they were just tossed in to fit the 5x5 model. The thing is, I would have expected 2e to nail their role down more, not keep them just as wishy-washy as they were in 1e when 2e has very clearly defined the ephemeral entity metaphysics. The 5x5 model doesn't fly as a justification for their existence any more, especially because Promethean 2e isn't even 5x5, so they should be working harder to justify themselves, but they don't seem to be. </div> </div> </div> But the Ulgan did have their fans in 1e, so cutting them from the game isn't exactly viable either. Like or hate them, they're part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T07:56:11-07:00","id":949311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, you have to understand that because of the 1e version's focus on spirits, the Ulgan was given a pseudo-shaman vibe over time. A revisal of the Ulgan will reise a huge chunk of the Lineage. So, the question becomes - how much of a change do you have before it becomes something completely different? And how desirable is it to make those changes and remove a character splat as opposed to keeping it as is? The writers decided to keep the shaman part.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's fine to keep the shaman vibe. It's a choice, and a valid one, but the book should commit to it, and I don't get the impression that it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't know about that. If its something that's firmly being changed, then its something that should be errata'd here as well. We're probably dealing with writer confusion, due to 1) constant confusion throughout multiple books, and 2) crossover from cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Ghostegate is being re-worded to reflect the fact that Twilight is a state of being, not a place. Creatures and objects that pass through a ghostgate aren't &quot;transported to the Twilight&quot;, they're transformed into ghost-attuned Twilight ephemera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe? The CofD isn't a highly technical game in the first place - it has a high focus on natural language.</div> </div> </div> </div>Natural language is all well and good, but a spirit is a specific thing in CofD, and CofD has a term for the more general category of thing that spirits are a part of. Language doesn't have to be technical to be consistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said the same thing about Mage 2e being stuck in 1e's metaphysics, and the answer back to me was &quot;that's just crossover stuff, and doesn't matter.&quot; I think the same kind of thought process is applying here.<br /> <br /> As near as I can tell, 2e is updating individual game lines to be internally consistant with the new rules and changes via game line supplements, and the rest of the so-called metaphysics (remember that each game line is technically stand alone) don't really apply. They're updating the game as it was writen before all those earlier changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like I said, the &quot;ectoplasm&quot; vs. &quot;ephemera&quot; as the name for the Ulgans' Humour is kind of a nitpick, and something I would be willing to overlook if they were otherwise more consistent about their relationship to ephemera. As it stands currently though, it's just one more thing muddying the issue of whether Ulgan are connected to spirit ephemera, ghost ephemera, both, neither, or what.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I do agree with you that there should be greater changes made. I think that some of the game lines coming out are doubling down on mistakes and oWoD carryovers instead of updating everything to the new, general CofD design. But I get the feeling that's not the design goal here.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first line that has given me that impression, personally, but I get where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I can tell, it was an attempt to make a more sin-eater-necromancer-esk type as opposed to the werewolf-esk-shaman style that the Ulgan currently has. Mind you, shamans deal heavily with ghosts too, so its kind of a moot point. In theory, it is absolutely possible to have a more Underworld focused prommie, but that doesn't change that the Ulgan deals with ghosts as well. Not exclusively (I didn't get that impression from the Bestowments), but ghosts are there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. In one place it is implied by contrast with Extempore that Ulgan are more associated with spirits than with ghosts. On another place it is stated that they are closely associated with ghosts and no mention of spirits is made. Even if you don't see these passages as directly contradictory, you've got to admit that it's at least not very clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And honestly, I think that's just a question of writer style and impression. I assume we're talking about two different writers. So, yes, I do think it should be brushed over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the developers job to insure that the individual writers' work gels into a cohesive whole? If this was a first draft I would understand, but the fact that this inconsistency made it through two drafts, two development phases, approvals, and is now in the advance PDF tells me that this is a deeper issue than just two writers with different styles and impressions of how Ulgan are supposed to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949295#post949295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the whole &quot;Lineage elements&quot; has really been downplayed a lot in 2e to the point that it only comes up when talking about regaining pyros. So, without 1e's understanding of the matter, I can see where it would feel off. <br /> <br /> But the Ulgan did have their fans in 1e, so cutting them from the game isn't exactly viable either. Like or hate them, they're part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't think they should be cut from the game, sorry if I gave that impression. I just think they should have a more developed identity. As it is, they're still stuck in 1e's nebulous &quot;kinda spirit-y, kinda ghost-y&quot; non-identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-12-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T09:07:55-07:00","id":949345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949311#post949311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fine to keep the shaman vibe. It's a choice, and a valid one, but the book should commit to it, and I don't get the impression that it does.</div> </div> </div> </div> I fail to see why it should comment on it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, Ghostegate is being re-worded to reflect the fact that Twilight is a state of being, not a place. Creatures and objects that pass through a ghostgate aren't &quot;transported to the Twilight&quot;, they're transformed into Twilight. </div> </div> </div> Meh. The fact its still a gate is going to leave confusion. Such a minor word change isn't going to help much. You walk through a portal. It acts just like hopping to the other side of the Gauntlet for getting around things in the physical world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Natural language is all well and good, but a spirit is a specific thing in CofD, and CofD has a term for the more general category of thing that spirits are a part of. Language doesn't have to be technical to be consistent. </div> </div> </div> You'll have to take it up with the developers, then. I remember when the 2e Khaibit came out and there was confusion over the world &quot;spirit&quot; there. Eventually it was clarified that the intent was anything that's ephemeral or ephemeral-like (arguably including qashmallim). I know there's debate over what &quot;spirit&quot; means in terms of CtL contracts like Inanimate Communication, and the Huntsmen are tenatively called &quot;spirits of the hunt&quot; despite zero connection to the <i>Hisil</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that its something that should or should not happen, just that it does happen. I'm not a lead or a developer, so its out of my hands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, like I said, the &quot;ectoplasm&quot; vs. &quot;ephemera&quot; as the name for the Ulgans' Humour is kind of a nitpick, and something I would be willing to overlook if they were otherwise more consistent about their relationship to ephemera. As it stands currently though, it's just one more thing muddying the issue of whether Ulgan are connected to spirit ephemera, ghost ephemera, both, neither, or what. </div> </div> </div> All the above. If its in Twilight, its fair game. There's a number of abilities in the game that work like that, and this is one of them. Spirit, ghost, angel, and even goetic (assuming a Mage crossover, since they don't exist outside that game).<br /> <br /> I get the impression that you're trying to divide things into a specific holes here. You can deal with spirits OR with ghosts OR with angels, etc. That's not what's going on. Such divisions aren't necessary. You deal with them all at once. Take Vampire, for instance - both the Khaibit and the strix, once they gain an &quot;interact with Twilight&quot; ability, they can affect anything, regardless of what kind of entity or object it is. Yes, Twilight Form strix can eat angels. Prime Arcana in Mage can affect ghosts, spirits and goetics all at once. The Ulgan is just another of the same kind, dealing with everything at once.<br /> <br /> Is it possible that the above is the source of confusion? If you think in terms of being general &quot;essence/ephemera&quot; instead of a specific wavelength, does it become clearer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if you don't see these passages as directly contradictory, you've got to admit that it's at least not very clear. </div> </div> </div> In light of the whole &quot;visiting the Underworld when you die&quot; stick, I don't think its unclear or contradictory at all. Sorry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, I don't think they should be cut from the game, sorry if I gave that impression. I just think they should have a more developed identity. As it is, they're still stuck in 1e's nebulous &quot;kinda spirit-y, kinda ghost-y&quot; non-identity. </div> </div> </div> But they do have an identity. They reflect the stories of shamans in the wilderness torn apart and reborn through their trials, as well as hints of sacrifical wickermen sacrificed to gods and spriits for good harvests. Spiritual constructs for dealing with ephemeral matters. Not everyone thinks that the identity fits into Promethean as is, but its definitely an identity.<br /> <br /> EDIT - its possible that I filled in holes with my previous knowledge of the game, but I can't help my unconscious there. I don't know if the book actually is contradictory or not, but I don't see it based on my understanding of the Ulgan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-12-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T09:42:50-07:00","id":949362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I fail to see why it should comment on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not comment on it, commit to it. If their schtick is supposed to be that they're shamans, that shtick should be followed through on rather than just vaguely present.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. The fact its still a gate is going to leave confusion. Such a minor word change isn't going to help much. You walk through a portal. It acts just like hopping to the other side of the Gauntlet for getting around things in the physical world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't doubt that it will, but the fact that the wording is being changed anyway is a pretty clear indication that (some of) the developers consider it important to present a consistent stance on the nature of Twilight, and I think it's worth following through on that stance in Promethean. If Mage is getting errata to make sure it's addressing Twilight in terms that are consistent with its metaphysical workings, Promethean should as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll have to take it up with the developers, then. I remember when the 2e Khaibit came out and there was confusion over the world &quot;spirit&quot; there. Eventually it was clarified that the intent was anything that's ephemeral or ephemeral-like (arguably including qashmallim). I know there's debate over what &quot;spirit&quot; means in terms of CtL contracts like Inanimate Communication, and the Huntsmen are tenatively called &quot;spirits of the hunt&quot; despite zero connection to the <i>Hisil</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one thing to describe the Huntsmen and other beings of the Wyrd that have no tie-in to Twilight or Ephemera as spirits; that's confusing on the order of using the word Demon to describe like twelve different things. It's another thing to use spirit to mean &quot;any kind of ephemeral entity&quot; when there's already a term for ephemeral entities. That's confusing on the order of calling rectangles squares.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying that its something that should or should not happen, just that it does happen. I'm not a lead or a developer, so its out of my hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, sure. I'm not asking you personally to change it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All the above. If its in Twilight, its fair game. There's a number of abilities in the game that work like that, and this is one of them. Spirit, ghost, angel, and even goetic (assuming a Mage crossover, since they don't exist outside that game).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine if that's the intent, my point is that the text does a poor job of communicating that to someone who isn't already familiar with the Ulgan's shtick from 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the impression that you're trying to divide things into a specific holes here. You can deal with spirits OR with ghosts OR with angels, etc. That's not what's going on. Such divisions aren't necessary. You deal with them all at once. Take Vampire, for instance - both the Khaibit and the strix, once they gain an &quot;interact with Twilight&quot; ability, they can affect anything, regardless of what kind of entity or object it is. Yes, Twilight Form strix can eat angels. Prime Arcana in Mage can affect ghosts, spirits and goetics all at once. The Ulgan is just another of the same kind, dealing with everything at once.<br /> <br /> Is it possible that the above is the source of confusion? If you think in terms of being general &quot;essence/ephemera&quot; instead of a specific wavelength, does it become clearer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, your earlier description of Ulgan as associated with ephemera as a substance or element already pretty much cleared that up for me. I got that they are meant to be connected to any and all types of ephemera, not to one particular category of ephemeral entity. I definitely appreciate that explanation. What's bugging me is that the book makes it seem in places like they are specifically associated with one type of ephemeral entity or another (usually spirits or ghosts), to the exclusion of other types, when that's apparently not the intent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In light of the whole &quot;visiting the Underworld when you die&quot; stick, I don't think its unclear or contradictory at all. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read both of the quotes I referenced? Just curious, because I don't see any way to interpret them both that isn't conflicting. One says that emphasizing ghosts over spirits can differentiate an Extempore from an Ulgan. Another says that Ulgan are more closely associated with ghosts and the underworld than Osirians. How do you reconcile these two facts? If Ulgans are connected to ephemera in general and not to Hisil spirits to the exclusion of ghosts, how can associating a character with ghosts differentiate them from Ulgan? And why is their Bestowment section so hyper-focused on ghosts and the underworld specifically instead of on Twilight and ephemera like it is in (some) other places?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they do have an identity. They reflect the stories of shamans in the wilderness torn apart and reborn through their trials, as well as hints of sacrifical wickermen sacrificed to gods and spriits for good harvests. Spiritual constructs for dealing with ephemeral matters. Not everyone thinks that the identity fits into Promethean as is, but its definitely an identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm saying is, the presentation of that identity is extremely muddled. I didn't get that impression of them at all from the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949345#post949345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT - its possible that I filled in holes with my previous knowledge of the game, but I can't help my unconscious there. I don't know if the book actually is contradictory or not, but I don't see it based on my understanding of the Ulgan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get the impression that is precisely the source of our misunderstanding. Thank you for sharing your insight though, it has definitely helped me better understand the intent behind the Ulgan, even if I don't think that intent is clearly communicated in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-12-2016, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:02:06-07:00","id":949374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949362#post949362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read both of the quotes I referenced? Just curious, because I don't see any way to interpret them both that isn't conflicting.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, I did. You can make an Extempore that's hyper focused on being like a Sin-Eater, to the point they only deal in ghosts and the Underworld, breach the gates, raise the dead, cross rivers, etc. A specialist instead of the Ulgan generalist. Its like that one Extempore example that modified the Frankenstein Bestowment to being more specialized in certain situations - more powerful but applicable in fewer instances. <br /> <br /> For instance, a character could have the power to interact with ghosts and raise their rank to 2 automatically, breaking any rank 1 ghosts out of their loops. Much more useful for dealing with ghosts than the regular Ulgan power, but doesn't negate what the Ulgan can do with ghosts at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thank you for sharing your insight though, it has definitely helped me better understand the intent behind the Ulgan, even if I don't think that intent is clearly communicated in the text. </div> </div> </div> Glad I could help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:03:22-07:00","id":949376,"title":"","content":"I think solution would be to consistly pointing that Ulgans are connected to 'Ephemera' as Humors - but split over particular beings connected. So shaman ones are connected to spirits. Then use 'Orpheans' connected to ghosts ( I do not know where they <i>were </i>described, but the where <b>somewhere</b> in 1E books ) mark them as new nickname, like Riven are for spirits. Both groups would then work generally on 'Ephemera', but most will spirit or ghost dedicated. Later devs could add next Ulgans of other kinds infused with 'Ephemera', not making them Extempore from start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:20:47-07:00","id":949383,"title":"","content":"Just got idea - Dreamborns would make great Ulgans made of goetia-related ephemera! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:40:58-07:00","id":949401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949374#post949374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, I did. You can make an Extempore that's hyper focused on being like a Sin-Eater, to the point they only deal in ghosts and the Underworld, breach the gates, raise the dead, cross rivers, etc. A specialist instead of the Ulgan generalist. Its like that one Extempore example that modified the Frankenstein Bestowment to being more specialized in certain situations - more powerful but applicable in fewer instances.<br /> <br /> For instance, a character could have the power to interact with ghosts and raise their rank to 2 automatically, breaking any rank 1 ghosts out of their loops. Much more useful for dealing with ghosts than the regular Ulgan power, but doesn't negate what the Ulgan can do with ghosts at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, if the intent is ghost specialist as opposed to ephemeral generalist, why does it contrast the ghost affinity with an affinity for &quot;the spirits of the wild&quot; instead of with &quot;ephemeral beings&quot;, or &quot;all creatures of twilight&quot;, or heck, even just &quot;other kinds of spirit&quot; if they don't want to give up using spirit as a generalized term? The &quot;of the wild&quot; part seems to imply a specialization towards spirits of the Hisil in contrast to the specialization towards ghosts of the dead, and that's inconsistent with the Ulgan's intent as ephemeral generalists.<br /> <br /> And, again, why is the Ulgan Bestowment section so highly focused on ghosts and the underworld? The way it's written makes them sound like the ghost specialist that is supposed to serve as a way to distinguish an ectoplasmic Extempore from an Ulgan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949374#post949374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad I could help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-12-2016, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:42:36-07:00","id":949403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949376#post949376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think solution would be to consistly pointing that Ulgans are connected to 'Ephemera' as Humors - but split over particular beings connected. So shaman ones are connected to spirits. Then use 'Orpheans' connected to ghosts ( I do not know where they <i>were </i>described, but the where <b>somewhere</b> in 1E books ) mark them as new nickname, like Riven are for spirits. Both groups would then work generally on 'Ephemera', but most will spirit or ghost dedicated. Later devs could add next Ulgans of other kinds infused with 'Ephemera', not making them Extempore from start.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be a cool way to approach it, for sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T11:12:17-07:00","id":949432,"title":"","content":"It seems pretty clear to me that we're just not going to agree here. I'll just write down my personal impressions and slip out here - I'm not even going to be playing the game, most likely, since I've become rather uncomfortable with certain other aspects. So, good luck with your games!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949401#post949401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, if the intent is ghost specialist as opposed to ephemeral generalist, why does it contrast the ghost affinity with an affinity for &quot;the spirits of the wild&quot; instead of with &quot;ephemeral beings&quot;, or &quot;all creatures of twilight&quot;, or heck, even just &quot;other kinds of spirit&quot; if they don't want to give up using spirit as a generalized term? The &quot;of the wild&quot; part seems to imply a specialization towards spirits of the Hisil in contrast to the specialization towards ghosts of the dead, and that's inconsistent with the Ulgan's intent as ephemeral generalists.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Ulgan, and the Copper Refinement by extension of the stereotype, in 1e were kind of luddites. They were stereotypical wilderness style guru types. The writer probably focused on that stereotype when writing his bit. In my experience, whenever someone is trying to compare one splat to another, far too often they reduce the second splat to simplistic stereotypes. And the books are as full of them as these very forums are. We even have sections called Steroetypes in the books!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, again, why is the Ulgan Bestowment section so highly focused on ghosts and the underworld? The way it's written makes them sound like the ghost specialist that is supposed to serve as a way to distinguish an ectoplasmic Extempore from an Ulgan. </div> </div> </div> Because the Prometheans as a whole have a new connection to the Underworld from when they die the first time, and this time the writer is choosing to focus on that new connection instead of previous stereotypes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T11:20:44-07:00","id":949435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949432#post949432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems pretty clear to me that we're just not going to agree here. I'll just write down my personal impressions and slip out here - I'm not even going to be playing the game, most likely, since I've become rather uncomfortable with certain other aspects. So, good luck with your games!</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool, thank you for sharing your insights even though you're not comfortable with other aspects of the game (side note: now you've got me curious, but this isn't the place). I think I've expressed my perspective adequately and it would be uncouth of me to try to pick apart your impressions when you wish to step away from the discussion, so I'm happy to let that exchange stand as it is. Best of luck in your games as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T12:09:23-07:00","id":949462,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to me that the Ulgan didn't use the actual fifth Greek Element way back when Promethean came out \u2014 Aether. It probably wouldn't change their concept much, but aesthetically it's a prettier word (YMMV). I'm curious if that was a design choice or just an oversight.<br /> <br /> Edit: On closer inspection (i.e., reading my copy of 1e), they did in fact, and I'm mixing up Humour and Element. That's what I get for posting this shortly after getting up...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 08-12-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:18:19-07:00","id":949601,"title":"","content":"Huh, that's odd, I liked the Ulgen a lot better in 2e than I did in 1e. Maybe they just had time to grow on me. I do like Wyrd's suggestion though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T16:34:40-07:00","id":949614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949601#post949601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, that's odd, I liked the Ulgen a lot better in 2e than I did in 1e. Maybe they just had time to grow on me. I do like Wyrd's suggestion though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't dislike them, I was just struggling to grasp their niche, as it was unclear to me if they were supposed to specialize in one or more particular types of ephemeral entity or not, and if so which one(s).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T18:22:47-07:00","id":949677,"title":"","content":"I want to address some of this, but it's difficult for a couple of reasons, chief among them that this is a tangle of related questions rather than one straightforward dealie. Proceeding as best I can on low sleep reserves:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think if they're not specifically supposed to be associated with the ghostly frequency of Twilight, then ephemera would be a better name for their Humour than ectoplasm. </div> </div> </div>Where this in particular runs into a problem is that &quot;ectoplasm&quot; has a real-world-and-echoed-here-in-the-game context that means more than &quot;ghost stuff.&quot; Ectoplasm is a substance related to the human body (or at least some specific kinds of human bodies) that facilitates the manifestation of otherworldly occult phenomena, most notably ghosts but also any other sort of being that you might see a spiritual medium call to dwell in them. The ectoplasmic humour is stuff which humans can theoretically produce that gives ephemeral beings a grip on our world, not the substance of other worlds itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the matter of &quot;why spirits?&quot; Well, that gets into one of those things that's tricky to grok except in aggregate. This is going to get a little rambly, but please try to bear with me:<br /> <br /> Much like Mage 2e highlights about ghosts, spirits only really suit the definition of &quot;[animistic/chthonic] reflections of [concepts/people]&quot; in the case of fairly basic and/or hyperfocused specimens. Setting aside the greater Celestines and their Big Recognizable Core Symbols, powerful spirits' portfolios become increasingly useless as guidelines for their psychology as they approach a critical mass of symbolism; spirit-nobles' spheres of influence are important as historical and political considerations, and they're the ones who tend to make it out of the Shadow. Lookaway Quickly may be a spirit of shame and unacknowledged wrongdoing in a general sense, but it's far more salient that it's a monster themed towards those qualities and their impact on its surroundings, whose ability to remain in this world is feeding on the Disquiet your Galateid throngmate is engendering. That's how spirits generally tend to become relevant to a setting whose main characters don't have the luxury of going into the Shadow on a regular basis \u2014 they're less clouds of living resonance and more ways the world echoes themes back at itself.<br /> <br /> Relatedly, the Ulgans' primary historical role as shamans has a little more push toward spirits than ghosts for the simple reason that they cause more trouble in ways that call for more esoteric methods of negotiating than the personalized monomanias of a Mane or Lemure. It's generally better to have the weird hermit you keep out of the village proper deal with the problems that arise from the wilderness being strange and terrifying and Outside than to call on them to talk dirty laundry with something you can keep away with proper burial rites and a heaping helping of salt. The Shadow is just about the leakiest otherworld in the greater Chronicles of Darkness and its principal means of ingress to our world are specifically oriented around places nobody much goes to, which are a lot harder for a community to keep an eye on all of than the sites of bloody battles and mass murder and so on. On that note, the Ulgans' Orphean interpretation is still more broadly focused on the mysterious nature of the land of the dead and the things that dwell there than on the sort of stuff that keeps a newborn ghost anchored, which means the type of ghost that an Ulgan is likely to deal with outside the Underworld is roughly similar to the kind of spirit that they're likely to deal with outside the Shadow: powerful, storied, often too solid to ignore, generally given over to the common supernatural tendencies that make them even remotely predictable.<br /> <br /> The Shadow is a landscape made up of the living thematic resonances of the material world and their interaction, but this fact serves as a point of interface with concerned parties from the material world, not the whole of its definition, and it's farther away the nearer you are to a lot of other people. The Ulgans were made, broadly speaking, to deal with the strange invisible monsters of myth and folklore so that someone else didn't have to, and that role isolates them in a simultaneous cause-and-effect relation to their ability to interact with (and therefore become entangled with) the invisible monsters that everyone stays away from, which serves as the core of the Lineage's typical desire for humanity.<br /> <br /> Ghosts could be broadly considered reflective of a similar role to the Ulgan through traditions like the graveyard watcher or their common association with things people shy away from, but a ghost is an inhuman thing that thinks it's human and stands to get less human over time, whereas a spirit is an inhuman thing that looks at humans as resources and thinks like a predator crossed with a supercomputer; one of these things is more obviously a recurring Threat to make a supernatural guardian against, but Bad Stuff comes out of the deadlands as well and there's no real thematic reason to draw a line between the two for the purposes of a gameline where the handling methods are ultimately more or less the same save for the tenor of some of the rumors that surround a given monster.<br /> <br /> Ulgans deal with spirits-and-ghost-but-mostly-spirits because those are the two most common varieties of ephemeral being that come from the closest ephemeral-being-harboring realms to the material world but one is a lot less location-locked than the other by both metaphysics and inclination.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:27:46-07:00","id":949853,"title":"","content":"Just want to respond to this, since it's unanswered.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949401#post949401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, again, why is the Ulgan Bestowment section so highly focused on ghosts and the underworld? The way it's written makes them sound like the ghost specialist that is supposed to serve as a way to distinguish an ectoplasmic Extempore from an Ulgan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually not.<br /> <br /> There 5 paragraphs in the Ulgan Bestowments section, only 2 of them mention ghosts <i>at all</i>, and only the first one appears to use them as more than an example. The actual mechanics are about <i>Twilight</i>, not ghosts.<br /> <br /> What's actually going on is that the first paragraph is contrasting Osirans with Ulgans. That's not the worst choice: this is the section where they talk about how one Lineage differs from another, after all. But it means that, since Osirans have a death focus, the contrast ends up talking about the border between life and death, instead of the border between flesh and spirit.<br /> <br /> A ghost, for an Osiran, is this strange and occasional entity they mess with from time to time, usually with purpose and intent. A ghost, for an Ulgan, is this persistent, annoying neighbor that just hangs out all the time. A spirit, for an Osiran, is something of an irrelevance. For an Ulgan, it's... a... persistent, annoying neighbor.<br /> <br /> I agree that it's pretty unclear, though; I would not have come to that conclusion without reading through this thread first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:45:18-07:00","id":949863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949853#post949853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There 5 paragraphs in the Ulgan Bestowments section, only 2 of them mention ghosts <i>at all</i>, and only the first one appears to use them as more than an example. The actual mechanics are about <i>Twilight</i>, not ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... Three of the five have the word ghost in them, and one of the remaining two talks about ripping aside the barriers set upon the living.<br /> <br /> Granted, the part that I was primarily referring to was the first two paragraphs, but those paragraphs <i>do</i> focus quite heavily on how Ulgan relate so much to ghosts and <i>dont</i> mention spirits at all, which <i>does</i> seem odd in contrast with the Extempore supposedly being able to differentiate themselves from Ulgan by focusing on ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949853#post949853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's actually going on is that the first paragraph is contrasting Osirans with Ulgans. That's not the worst choice: this is the section where they talk about how one Lineage differs from another, after all. But it means that, since Osirans have a death focus, the contrast ends up talking about the border between life and death, instead of the border between flesh and spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... <i>none</i> of the other Lineages Beatowments are introduced by contrasting them with another Lineage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/949130-what-s-up-with-the-ulgan?p=949853#post949853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost, for an Osiran, is this strange and occasional entity they mess with from time to time, usually with purpose and intent. A ghost, for an Ulgan, is this persistent, annoying neighbor that just hangs out all the time. A spirit, for an Osiran, is something of an irrelevance. For an Ulgan, it's... a... persistent, annoying neighbor.</div> </div> </div> </div>The section in question really doesn't communicate that to me. All it did was confuse me further as to what the nature of the Ulgans' connection with spirits/ghosts/etc. was supposed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:00:15-07:00","id":949904,"title":"","content":"Well, I will stick with my own retcon for book in 2E games until it will be totally invalid - <b>Ulgan is name for general, Ephemera based Humor Created Linage - in it are Riven and </b><b>Orpheans ( and probably Dreamborns of Australia )</b>, all related to main idea of Ephemera Humor, but specialized to one version of it. They all work more or less the same, they only have other 'focus' on ephemera entity they feel closest connection. Each this connection is highlighted by their individual Bestowment. Simple and elegant. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-13-2016, 03:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}